{"type":"system","subtype":"task_notification","task_id":"bylz73819","tool_use_id":"toolu_01WfmTYWxqwVtxGsGrFP7TEz","status":"completed","output_file":"/tmp/claude-441489/-scratch-users-kushinm-auto-psych-outer-loop-live-runs-run1-repo/95e9393f-44b7-4963-9143-59b6fc4d5645/tasks/bylz73819.output","summary":"Background command \"D=/scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/run1/data/subjective_randomness/experiment3/model_loop/iter_4/candidate_5\ncat << 'EOF' > $D/hypothesis.md\nRefinement of `capacity_blur_personal_antisymmetry` (statistically tied with the best): each person still has their own working-memory capacity, so their impression of which sequence looks more random decides the choice sharply for short pairs but is blurred for pairs whose length approaches or exceeds that capacity, and the impression is still judged by a personal ideal switching rate and sensitivity (lenient toward over-alternation), personal weights on imbalance and the longest streak, shared structural cues (final streak, mirror symmetry, complement symmetry, run-length variety, most lopsided stretch) and a personal guessing rate. The one change is replacing its personal weight on antisymmetry alone with the incumbent's personal pattern-detection gain: each person has one trait for noticing designed structure that scales all the structural cues together — so two separate personal sources of consistency (memory capacity, concentrated on long pairs, and general pattern noticing, concentrated on structured sequences) are estimated jointly, addressing the critique (surviving FDR) that people differ in how consistently they agree with the majority more than the incumbent's gain alone produces.\nEOF\necho capacity_blur_pattern_gain > $D/model_name.txt\npython3 - << 'PY'\nsrc=open(\"/scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/run1/data/subjective_randomness/experiment3/model_loop/models/capacity_blur_personal_antisymmetry.py\").read()\ndoc_end=src.index('\"\"\"',3)+3\nnewdoc='''\"\"\"Capacity blur with a personal pattern-detection gain.\n\nRefinement of `capacity_blur_personal_antisymmetry`: each person still holds\nboth sequences in working memory with their own capacity, so the comparison is\ndivided by sqrt(1 + (n / K_i)^2) and long pairs are judged less sharply by\nlow-capacity people; the impression is still a personal ideal switching rate\nand sensitivity (asymmetric tolerance), personal weights on imbalance and the\nlongest run, shared structural cues (final run, mirror symmetry, complement\nsymmetry, run-length variety, most lopsided stretch) and a personal lapse\nrate. The one change: instead of a personal weight on antisymmetry alone, one\npersonal pattern-detection gain (population-distributed, median 1) scales all\nstructural cues together, whose relative weights are shared.\n\"\"\"'''\nsrc=newdoc+src[doc_end:]\nold_chi=src[src.index(\"    # Shared penalty on complement symmetry\"):src.index(\"    # Shared fraction of the ideal-rate\")]\nsrc=src.replace(old_chi,'''    # Shared penalty on complement symmetry (positive: antisymmetric sequences look designed).\n    chi = pm.Normal(\"chi\", mu=0.0, sigma=1.5)\n\n    # Personal pattern-detection gain scaling all structural cues (median 1).\n    sigma_gain = pm.HalfNormal(\"sigma_gain\", sigma=0.7)\n    z_gain = pm.Normal(\"z_gain\", mu=0.0, sigma=1.0, shape=MAX_PARTICIPANTS)\n    gain = pm.math.exp(sigma_gain * z_gain)\n\n''')\nsrc=src.replace(\"    c = chi[participant_id]\\n\",\"    s = gain[participant_id]\\n\\n    def structure(endrun, palin, variety, lopsided, antisym):\\n        return -kappa * endrun - rho * palin + omega * variety - eta * lopsided - chi * antisym\\n\\n\")\nsrc=src.replace(\"- kappa * endrun_a - rho * palin_a + omega * variety_a - eta * lopsided_a - c * antisym_a\",\"+ s * structure(endrun_a, palin_a, variety_a, lopsided_a, antisym_a)\")\nsrc=src.replace(\"- kappa * endrun_b - rho * palin_b + omega * variety_b - eta * lopsided_b - c * antisym_b\",\"+ s * structure(endrun_b, palin_b, variety_b, lopsided_b, antisym_b)\")\nopen(\"/scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/run1/data/subjective_randomness/experiment3/model_loop/iter_4/candidate_5/candidate.py\",\"w\").write(src)\nPY\ngrep -n \"score_\\|structure\\|gain\\|chi\" $D/candidate.py\ncd /scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/runs/run1/repo && /scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/venv/bin/python -m src.pipelines.inner_loop.check_candidate --candidate-dir $D --responses /scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/run1/data/subjective_randomness/experiment3/model_loop/responses.csv 2>&1 | tail -5\" completed (exit code 0)","uuid":"bb5b5ba4-243d-4f12-ae2e-91400cea7104","session_id":"95e9393f-44b7-4963-9143-59b6fc4d5645"}
