{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfdvkbu72y5xTUoh7jTYb","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've written the candidate `capacity_blur_pattern_gain`, and it passes the self-check (`OK`; smoke-fit ELPD-LOO −3452.7). The check didn't cover novelty against the other models, the convergence gate or the 30-minute fit limit, so those are still open.\n\n**Which model I refined:** `capacity_blur_personal_antisymmetry`, the closest live model to the incumbent (10.9 ± 6.8 nats behind, a statistical tie).\n\n**What I changed:** I took out its personal weight on antisymmetry and put in the incumbent's personal pattern-detection gain. That gain is one trait per person that scales all the structural cues together: final streak, mirror symmetry, complement symmetry, run-length variety and the most lopsided stretch. Each person's working-memory capacity still blurs the comparison on long pairs, and everything else in the model is unchanged.\n\n**Why:** the one critique result that survives the FDR is that people differ more than the incumbent predicts in how often they agree with the majority. This model gives that two separate personal sources, fitted together. Memory capacity mostly affects long pairs, and pattern-noticing mostly affects sequences with visible structure.\n\n**Risks at admission:**\n- **Unreliable PSIS-LOO:** the smoke fit had 9.1% of trials with Pareto k > 0.5, well above the 1% tolerance. This was a 1-chain, 100-draw run, so it may just be the short fit. The full fit may still come out unreliable, and then its ELPD-LOO is untrustworthy and it can't be the exported winner.\n- **Novelty gate:** predictions could sit within 0.002 RMSE of a live model, most likely the incumbent or the model I refined. I expect the capacity blur to keep it apart, because it changes how predictions depend on sequence length, but I haven't checked.\n\nAll three files (`hypothesis.md`, `model_name.txt`, `candidate.py`) are in `.../experiment3/model_loop/iter_4/candidate_5/`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2704,"cache_read_input_tokens":103142,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2704,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":7,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"95e9393f-44b7-4963-9143-59b6fc4d5645","uuid":"cae976d2-20a5-42e9-9e59-126ade7926c4","timestamp":"2026-10-02T19:01:53.720Z","request_id":"req_011CfdvkaggdwikGcxHQUpDk"}
